    {
      "id": "MJUe",
      "code_hash": "92ec0ec11b9cabf060e05c3f135eec1b",
      "outputs": [
        {
          "type": "data",
          "data": {
            "text/markdown": "<span class=\"markdown prose dark:prose-invert contents\"><h1 id=\"eddy-playground\">\ud83c\udf00 eddy playground</h1>\n<span class=\"paragraph\"><a href=\"https://pypi.org/project/tidaleddy/\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">eddy</a> is the TidalCycles pattern engine from\n<a href=\"https://codeberg.org/uzu/vortex\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">Vortex</a>, the Python port of TidalCycles (Strudel is\nits JavaScript sibling). Normally Tidal sends OSC to SuperCollider/SuperDirt. Here a\nsmall numpy synth (<code>eddy.marimo</code>) renders the pattern straight to audio instead, so\nnothing else needs installing.</span>\n<span class=\"paragraph\"><strong>How to play:</strong> press <strong>\u25b6 Play</strong>, then play with the code below it. It's a\n<a href=\"https://worrydream.com/Tangle/\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">Tangle</a>-style code editor built from\n<a href=\"https://github.com/koaning/wigglystuff\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">wigglystuff</a> widgets:</span>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>type:</strong> click any code to edit that line. <strong>\u21b5</strong> applies it, <strong>esc</strong> cancels, <strong>\u2191 \u2193</strong> move between lines.\n  \"+ add a layer\" adds a line, and an empty line is removed. <strong>\u270e edit as text</strong> edits (or pastes) the whole stack.</li>\n<li><strong>drag</strong> the blue numbers (shift = \u00d710, alt = \u00d70.1, or click one to type a value)</li>\n<li><strong>click</strong> a sound or scale name to cycle it, or \ud83d\udd0a to mute a layer</li>\n<li><strong>shape the path:</strong> the pad above the code is a loop you bend by dragging its knots. A dot rides it in\n  time with the music, and layers can follow the dot with <code>path.x</code>, <code>path.y</code> and <code>path.knots</code>.</li>\n</ul>\n<span class=\"paragraph\">Every change comes in on the next cycle and playback doesn't stop. <strong>\u25a0 Hush</strong> stops it.\nEdits live in the widget. To keep them, <strong>copy</strong> the stack as code, or paste it into\nthe editor cell's source. Re-running that cell resets it.</span></span>"
          }
        }
      ],
      "console": []
    },
