    {
      "id": "Hstk",
      "code_hash": "5d1d7b69b464387134cc23f9e1c02013",
      "outputs": [
        {
          "type": "data",
          "data": {
            "text/markdown": "<span class=\"markdown prose dark:prose-invert contents\"><h2 id=\"cheat-sheet\">Cheat sheet</h2>\n<table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th></th>\n<th></th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Drums</strong></td>\n<td><code>bd</code> <code>sn</code>/<code>sd</code> <code>hh</code> <code>oh</code> <code>cp</code> <code>rim</code> <code>cb</code> <code>lt</code> <code>mt</code> <code>ht</code> <code>cr</code> <code>perc</code>. Use <code>:n</code> or <code>.n()</code> for variants, e.g. <code>s(\"bd:2\")</code></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Synths</strong></td>\n<td><code>sine</code> <code>tri</code> <code>saw</code> <code>square</code> <code>supersaw</code> <code>superpiano</code> <code>pluck</code> <code>bass</code> <code>pad</code>. Pitch comes from <code>note</code> and/or <code>n</code></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Notes</strong></td>\n<td>Tidal convention: <code>0</code> = <code>c5</code> = middle C. Names look like <code>c</code>, <code>eb4</code>, <code>fs6</code>; numbers are semitones</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Controls</strong></td>\n<td><code>gain</code> <code>pan</code> <code>speed</code> <code>legato</code> <code>sustain</code> <code>attack</code> <code>release</code> <code>octave</code> <code>cutoff</code> <code>hcutoff</code> (Hz) <code>shape</code> <code>crush</code> <code>coarse</code> <code>room</code> <code>size</code> <code>delay</code> <code>delaytime</code> (s) <code>delayfeedback</code></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Mini-notation</strong></td>\n<td><code>~</code> rest \u00b7 <code>[a b]</code> group \u00b7 <code>a*3</code> \u00b7 <code>a/2</code> \u00b7 <code>&lt;a b&gt;</code> alternate \u00b7 <code>a(3,8)</code> euclid \u00b7 <code>a@3</code> \u00b7 <code>a _ b</code> \u00b7 <code>[a, b]</code> stack \u00b7 <code>a . b</code> \u00b7 <code>a?</code> maybe \u00b7 <code>a!3</code> repeat \u00b7 <code>a | b</code> either \u00b7 <code>{a b, c d e}</code> polymeter \u00b7 <code>0 .. 7</code> range</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Functions</strong></td>\n<td><code>.fast</code> <code>.slow</code> <code>.rev</code> <code>.every(n, f)</code> <code>.jux(rev)</code> <code>.iter(4)</code> <code>.superimpose(f)</code> <code>.degrade_by(.3)</code> <code>.sometimes(f)</code> <code>.segment(n)</code> <code>.struct()</code> <code>.mask()</code> <code>.early</code> <code>.late</code></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Signals</strong></td>\n<td><code>sine()</code> <code>saw()</code> <code>tri()</code> <code>square()</code> <code>rand()</code> <code>perlin()</code> <code>irand(8)</code>, all scaled with <code>.range(lo, hi)</code></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>The path</strong></td>\n<td><code>path.x</code> <code>path.y</code> are signals too (0 to 1, one lap of the path per loop). <code>path.knots</code> is a hit at every knot, for <code>.struct(path.knots)</code></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Scales</strong></td>\n<td><code>scale(\"minor\", \"0 2 4 7\")</code> turns scale steps into notes: <code>minpent</code> <code>majpent</code> <code>minor</code> <code>major</code> <code>dorian</code> <code>phrygian</code> <code>lydian</code> <code>mixolydian</code> <code>harmonic</code> <code>blues</code> <code>whole</code> <code>chromatic</code></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<span class=\"paragraph\"><strong>How this differs from Strudel:</strong> methods are snake_case (<code>degrade_by</code>, not\n<code>degradeBy</code>), signals are functions (<code>sine()</code>, not <code>sine</code>), and lambdas take\nthe place of arrow functions (<code>.sometimes(lambda p: p.speed(2))</code>).</span>\n<span class=\"paragraph\"><strong>Engine quirks to know about:</strong> you can't do arithmetic on control patterns\n(<code>n(\"0 2\") + 12</code> fails; write <code>n(sequence(0, 2) + 12)</code>), and <code>\"&lt;a b&gt;*8\"</code> plays\n<code>a b a b \u2026</code> as in Tidal (use <code>s(\"&lt;a b&gt;\").segment(8)</code> to hold each value for a cycle).</span></span>"
          }
        }
      ],
      "console": []
    },
    {
      "id": "nWHF",
      "code_hash": "673ad2d942805753d0f8233293a14394",
      "outputs": [
        {
          "type": "data",
          "data": {
            "text/markdown": "<span class=\"markdown prose dark:prose-invert contents\"><h2 id=\"things-to-try\">Things to try</h2>\n<span class=\"paragraph\">Paste any of these into the free-form cell or mute the editor's layers to hear them alone:</span>\n<div class=\"language-python codehilite\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"c1\"># the path as a bassline: the dot's height picks one of five low notes, twice per cycle</span>\n<span class=\"n\">extra</span> <span class=\"o\">=</span> <span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">scale</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"s2\">\"minpent\"</span><span class=\"p\">,</span> <span class=\"n\">path</span><span class=\"o\">.</span><span class=\"n\">y</span><span class=\"o\">.</span><span class=\"n\">range</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"mi\">0</span><span class=\"p\">,</span> <span class=\"mi\">5</span><span class=\"p\">)</span><span class=\"o\">.</span><span class=\"n\">segment</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"mi\">2</span><span class=\"p\">)))</span><span class=\"o\">.</span><span class=\"n\">s</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"s2\">\"bass\"</span><span class=\"p\">)</span><span class=\"o\">.</span><span class=\"n\">octave</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"mi\">3</span><span class=\"p\">)</span><span class=\"o\">.</span><span class=\"n\">legato</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"mf\">0.8</span><span class=\"p\">)</span>\n\n<span class=\"c1\"># every knot of the path plays a chord</span>\n<span class=\"n\">extra</span> <span class=\"o\">=</span> <span class=\"n\">note</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"s2\">\"[c,eb,g]\"</span><span class=\"p\">)</span><span class=\"o\">.</span><span class=\"n\">s</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"s2\">\"superpiano\"</span><span class=\"p\">)</span><span class=\"o\">.</span><span class=\"n\">struct</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">path</span><span class=\"o\">.</span><span class=\"n\">knots</span><span class=\"p\">)</span><span class=\"o\">.</span><span class=\"n\">room</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"mf\">0.4</span><span class=\"p\">)</span>\n\n<span class=\"c1\"># acid-ish bass with a cutoff sweep and some distortion</span>\n<span class=\"n\">extra</span> <span class=\"o\">=</span> <span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"s2\">\"0 0 12 0 3 0 10 7\"</span><span class=\"p\">)</span><span class=\"o\">.</span><span class=\"n\">s</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"s2\">\"saw\"</span><span class=\"p\">)</span><span class=\"o\">.</span><span class=\"n\">octave</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"mi\">3</span><span class=\"p\">)</span><span class=\"o\">.</span><span class=\"n\">legato</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"mf\">0.5</span><span class=\"p\">)</span> \\\n    <span class=\"o\">.</span><span class=\"n\">cutoff</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">sine</span><span class=\"p\">()</span><span class=\"o\">.</span><span class=\"n\">range</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"mi\">200</span><span class=\"p\">,</span> <span class=\"mi\">3000</span><span class=\"p\">)</span><span class=\"o\">.</span><span class=\"n\">slow</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"mi\">2</span><span class=\"p\">))</span><span class=\"o\">.</span><span class=\"n\">shape</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"mf\">0.4</span><span class=\"p\">)</span>\n\n<span class=\"c1\"># stereo trick: jux plays a reversed copy on the right</span>\n<span class=\"n\">extra</span> <span class=\"o\">=</span> <span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">run</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"mi\">8</span><span class=\"p\">))</span><span class=\"o\">.</span><span class=\"n\">s</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"s2\">\"pluck\"</span><span class=\"p\">)</span><span class=\"o\">.</span><span class=\"n\">jux</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">rev</span><span class=\"p\">)</span><span class=\"o\">.</span><span class=\"n\">room</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"mf\">0.4</span><span class=\"p\">)</span>\n\n<span class=\"c1\"># randomness with a fixed seed per cycle, so every loop sounds the same</span>\n<span class=\"n\">extra</span> <span class=\"o\">=</span> <span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">irand</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"mi\">12</span><span class=\"p\">)</span><span class=\"o\">.</span><span class=\"n\">segment</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"mi\">8</span><span class=\"p\">))</span><span class=\"o\">.</span><span class=\"n\">s</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"s2\">\"superpiano\"</span><span class=\"p\">)</span><span class=\"o\">.</span><span class=\"n\">sometimes</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"k\">lambda</span> <span class=\"n\">p</span><span class=\"p\">:</span> <span class=\"n\">p</span><span class=\"o\">.</span><span class=\"n\">octave</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"mi\">6</span><span class=\"p\">))</span><span class=\"o\">.</span><span class=\"n\">room</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"mf\">0.4</span><span class=\"p\">)</span>\n</code></pre></div></span>"
          }
        }
